{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory contains `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a stub `card_impl.py` (a class extending `CardImpl` with `pass`) to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, don't read whole) for rules. The agent is expected/encouraged to make additive changes to the engine to implement new keywords/mechanics.\n\n   Explicit constraints (MUST be preserved):\n   - Do NOT modify, add to, or delete any files under `workspace/engine_tests/` (read-only; runner uses its own authoritative copies; modifying them only misleads, does not change score).\n   - Do NOT modify or delete existing FDN reference test files at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (read for examples only).\n   - Engine modifications are ADDITIVE-ONLY: may add new methods/classes/helpers/files in `engine/` and may modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — would break grader imports and zero the score).\n   - Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n   - The agent's own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Run tests from workspace root with `pytest` (pytest.ini sets `python_files = test_*.py tests.py`, 5-min timeout).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine with layered architecture: CardImpl hierarchy, GameState, Stack, TriggerManager, ReplacementManager, EffectManager (7-layer continuous effects), CombatState, ManaPool.\n   - Card hooks: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)` (generic-only reduction, clamped ≥0, colored pips never reduced), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)` (returns list of `TargetRequirement`), `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()`, `get_modes()`, `get_loyalty_abilities()` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities()` (Land).\n   - Triggered events (`engine/events.py`): typed dataclasses; subclass matching (parent type matches subclass instances).\n   - Replacement effects: \"instead\" semantics, `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (with subclasses CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice), `destination` mutable string (\"graveyard\"/\"exile\"/\"hand\"/\"library\"), `prevented` flag.\n   - Mana: `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (list of Color), cast pipeline sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`. NOTE: total mana spent is NOT currently tracked.\n   - Converge: `colors_spent` set as list by real cast pipeline; FDN tests set it as int count directly; impls must handle this duality.\n   - Targets: `chosen_targets` set on card at resolve time by `_resolve_spell` from `StackObject.targets`; FDN convention helper `_get_chosen_target` reads `chosen_targets` then falls back to `_resolve_target`.\n   - Counterspells: target a `StackObject` (zone=Zone.STACK), `can_cast` checks stack, `on_resolve` removes from stack and moves card to graveyard.\n   - Free casting: `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` exists for casting without paying mana from any zone.\n   - Spell copy: `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` for casualty-type effects.\n   - Loyalty abilities: `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` returned by `get_loyalty_abilities()`; `LoyaltyAbilityInstance` + `activate_ability` enforce sorcery-speed + once-per-turn; loyalty targeting uses `_resolve_target`.\n   - Continuous effects: `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`/`DURATION_PERMANENT`, `Layer` IntEnum, `SubLayer`; `effect_manager.add(...)`; `_reset_characteristics()` resets each cycle (override to reapply static effects like protection — see Progenitus pattern).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md` & `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`: Rules/constraints and directory layout. FDN cards with tests.py: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244.\n   - SOS card specs (all read). Summaries:\n     - SOS 1 The Dawning Archaic: Legendary Creature—Avatar, {10}, 7/7, Reach. Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard. Attack trigger: may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard free; if it would go to graveyard, exile instead. (class `TheDawningArchaic`)\n     - SOS 4 Together as One: Sorcery {6}. Converge — target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life; X = colors of mana spent. (class `TogetherAsOne`)\n     - SOS 13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares: Creature—Cat Cleric {1}{W}{W} 3/3 // Instant {W}; ETB: target player creates 1/1 W/B Inkling flier; if opponent controls more creatures, becomes \"prepared\". Keyword Prepared. (class `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`)\n     - SOS 57 Mana Sculpt: Instant {1}{U}{U}. Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana spent to cast that spell at beginning of your next main phase. (class `ManaSculpt`)\n     - SOS 97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer: Legendary Planeswalker—Ral {1}{B}{B}, loyalty 3. +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard; −2 return creature card MV≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X = heads). (class `RalZarekGuestLecturer`)\n     - SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone: Sorcery—Lesson {5}{R}{R}. Exile from top of library until total MV≥4; may cast any number free. Paradigm. (class `ImprovisationCapstone`)\n     - SOS 201 Lorehold, the Historian: Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon {3}{R}{W} 5/5 Flying Haste. Each instant/sorcery in hand has miracle {2}. Each opponent's upkeep, may discard a card to draw. (class `LoreholdTheHistorian`)\n     - SOS 226 Silverquill, the Disputant: Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon {2}{W}{B} 4/4 Flying Vigilance. Each instant/sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (class `SilverquillTheDisputant`)\n     - SOS 245 Witherbloom, the Balancer: Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Flying Deathtouch. Affinity for creatures (this + your instant/sorcery spells). (class `WitherbloomTheBalancer`)\n     - SOS 257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex: Land. {T}: Add {C}; {T}, Pay 1 life: add any color for instant/sorcery only; {5}: becomes 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this gets +1/+0 EOT\", still a land. (class `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`)\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py`: Base classes — CardImpl, Creature (base_power/toughness, modified_power/toughness, power/toughness properties incl counters, `_reset_characteristics`), Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker (starting_loyalty, loyalty, get_loyalty_abilities), Land (can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities). Dataclasses: Mode, ActivatedAbility, LoyaltyAbility, ManaAbility, ContinuousEffect.\n   - `/workspace/engine/types.py`: Color (with W/U/B/R/G aliases), ManaType (incl COLORLESS), Zone, Phase, Step, CardType, Supertype, Keyword (Flag: FLYING, REACH, HASTE, DEATHTOUCH, VIGILANCE, etc.), ManaCost (`parse`, `cmc`, generic/pips/x_count/hybrid), TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `_resolve_spell` (calls on_resolve then moves permanent→battlefield or instant/sorcery→graveyard via move_to_zone), `play_land`, `get_cost_reduction`/`_apply_cost_reduction`, `is_sorcery_speed`, `can_cast_at_instant_speed`. Cast pipeline sets `card.colors_spent` after payment.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py`: `move_zone` (deletes `colors_spent` on zone change), `move_to_zone` (replacement handling for leaving-battlefield, fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies, registers triggers/replacement effects + fires ETB on entering).\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py`: helpers `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card`, `discard`, `create_token` (sets is_token, fires ETB, registers triggers), `add_counter`/`remove_counter` (supports \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\", generic dict), `tap`/`untap`, `create_game`, `run_game`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py`: `declare_attackers_step` (taps unless vigilance, sets is_attacking — does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent), `declare_blockers_step`, `combat_damage_step`, `end_combat_step`, CombatState.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py`: `activate_ability`, `ActivatedAbilityInstance`, `LoyaltyAbilityInstance`, `tap_cost`, loyalty tracking (`clear_loyalty_tracking`).\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py`: legend rule, lethal damage, zero toughness, etc.\n   - `/workspace/engine/continuous_effects.py`: EffectManager + Layer/SubLayer + ContinuousEffect.\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py`: `create_game(deck1,deck2,*,scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game,player_index,*,battlefield,hand,graveyard,life,mana)`, `cast_spell(game,player_index,card_name,targets)`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`, `card_colors`.\n   - FDN reference impls read (key patterns):\n     - fdn_13 FleetingFlight: `get_targets` returns `[TargetRequirement(filter_fn=..., description=..., zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD)]`; `on_resolve` reads `chosen_targets`; uses `add_counter` + `_base_plus_one_counters` sync; ContinuousEffect for flying EOT.\n     - fdn_205 WardensOfTheCycle: Converge — `self.colors_spent` int count in on_resolve, `range(count)` creates Saproling tokens via `create_token`.\n     - fdn_215 Bushwhack: modal via `get_modes()` + `self.chosen_mode`; library search + fight via `deal_damage`.\n     - fdn_244 Progenitus: `ProtectionAbility(quality='everything', predicate=lambda s: True)`, `_init_protection` reapplied in overridden `_reset_characteristics`; `register_replacement_effects` registers `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` with condition `event.card is source`, replacement shuffles into library and sets `event.prevented = True`.\n     - fdn_44 Kaito: Planeswalker pattern — `register_triggers` (DealsDamageTriggeredEvent), `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1, effect=_plus1, ...), ...]`; emblem via anonymous object + TriggerRegistration.\n     - fdn_153 EssenceScatter: counterspell — `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` removes from stack, moves card to graveyard; targets are StackObjects; `can_cast` checks stack.\n     - fdn_57 BlasphemousEdict & fdn_29 ArcaneEpiphany: `cost_reduction(game)` examples (generic-only; note engine clamps to generic).\n   - `/workspace/engine_tests/test_abilities.py`: shows ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance construction and activate_ability behavior — useful for understanding ability invocation in tests.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None yet — no code changes have been made; this has been pure exploration.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the engine does NOT fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (needed for SOS 1's attack trigger) or `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (needed for SOS 257's animated-creature \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\" trigger, and potentially others). Will need additive engine changes (fire AttacksTriggeredEvent in `declare_attackers_step`; fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in `cast_spell`).\n   - Identified that total \"amount of mana spent to cast a spell\" is not tracked (only colors). For SOS 57 (Mana Sculpt) will likely need to add e.g. `card.mana_spent` in the cast pipeline.\n   - Noted `colors_spent` is a list from the real pipeline but int in FDN converge tests — SOS 4 must handle both (use `len()` if list, else int).\n   - Noted `cost_reduction` only reduces generic mana — fine for SOS 1 ({10}) and SOS 245 (affinity reduces generic).\n   - No engine helpers exist for surveil/scry/miracle/affinity/casualty/paradigm/prepared — these must be built within card impls and/or with additive engine support.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System-reminder) Deferred tools available via ToolSearch (CronCreate, EnterPlanMode, NotebookEdit, TaskCreate, WebFetch, etc.) — must load schemas via ToolSearch before calling.\n   - (System-reminder) List of available skills (update-config, verify, code-review, simplify, run, init, review, security-review, etc.).\n   - Main task message: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Several repeated automated reminders to consider using Task tools (TaskCreate/TaskUpdate) for progress tracking.\n   - Final instruction: produce this summary (text only, no tools).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement all 10 SOS card_impl.py files (none done yet).\n   - Make additive engine changes to support: AttacksTriggeredEvent firing (combat.py), SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing (casting.py), tracking total mana spent for Mana Sculpt, and likely helpers for surveil, miracle, casualty, affinity, converge X, paradigm, prepared, coin flips/extra-turn-skip.\n   - Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` for local verification.\n   - Run `pytest` to verify nothing breaks and implementations work.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I had completed reading the engine and FDN reference cards and just ran a grep confirming which TriggeredEvents the engine fires. Key finding: the engine fires EntersBattlefield/LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies (zones.py), DealsDamage/LosesLife/GainsLife/DrawsCard (game.py), BeginningOfUpkeep (turn.py), but does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent, SpellCastTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent, EndStepTriggeredEvent, or EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent. I also confirmed no engine helpers exist for affinity/miracle/casualty/surveil/paradigm/prepared/convoke, and read fdn_29 (ArcaneEpiphany) as a `cost_reduction` example. No files have been edited or created yet. The next phase is designing and implementing each card with the necessary additive engine support.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementation, starting with the engine additions needed and the simpler cards. Directly in line with the task (\"Implement the following SOS cards... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics\"), the next concrete step is: add `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing to `declare_attackers_step` in `engine/combat.py` and `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` firing to `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free` in `engine/casting.py` (plus track total mana spent), then implement the cards in order of complexity (e.g., SOS 245 Witherbloom affinity via `cost_reduction`, SOS 4 Together as One converge, SOS 57 Mana Sculpt counterspell, SOS 1 attack trigger, then planeswalker SOS 97, then SOS 13/120/201/226/257). I should set up a Task list (TaskCreate) to track the 10 cards plus engine changes before editing, then verify with `pytest`. Before any edits I will re-confirm I am not touching `engine_tests/` or FDN `tests.py`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/735f529e-7bc8-4328-a211-d2f095818fd0.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"735f529e-7bc8-4328-a211-d2f095818fd0","uuid":"a36dc60e-7cf3-4730-8084-ce02e082be77","timestamp":"2026-06-04T09:46:39.670Z","isSynthetic":true}
