{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory contains `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a stub `card_impl.py` (a class extending `CardImpl`/subclass with `pass`) to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, do not read whole) for rules. The agent is explicitly \"expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics\" and is \"free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\" For engine API discovery, read source modules directly (engine/card.py, engine/events.py, engine/triggers.py, engine/replacement_effects.py, engine/zones.py).\n\n   Hard constraints (MUST be preserved verbatim):\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Do NOT modify or delete existing FDN reference test files at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (read for examples only).\n   - Engine modifications are ADDITIVE-ONLY: may add new methods/classes/helpers/files in `engine/` and may modify the bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — would break grader imports and zero the score).\n   - Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card directories.\n   - The agent's own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Run tests from workspace root with `pytest` (pytest.ini sets `python_files = test_*.py tests.py`, 5-min timeout).\n\n   Final message: produce this summary as TEXT ONLY (no tool calls).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Layered MTG engine: CardImpl hierarchy, GameState, Stack, TriggerManager, ReplacementManager, EffectManager (7-layer continuous effects), CombatState, ManaPool, DeterministicPlayer.\n   - Card hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)` (generic-only, clamped ≥0, only reduces generic — `get_cost_reduction` sets card.controller temporarily then restores), `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets` (returns list of `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`), `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, `get_loyalty_abilities` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities` (Land).\n   - Triggered events (engine/events.py): typed dataclasses; subclass matching via isinstance. Fired by engine: EntersBattlefield/LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies (zones.py), DealsDamage/LosesLife/GainsLife/DrawsCard (game.py), BeginningOfUpkeep (turn.py). NOT fired (defined but unused): SpellCastTriggeredEvent, AttacksTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent, EndStepTriggeredEvent, EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent.\n   - TriggerManager.fire_event: collects matching triggers, APNAP-orders, pushes StackObjects; returns early (no-op) if none match. TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller).\n   - Replacement effects: \"instead\" semantics. MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent (subclasses CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice), `.card` property, `destination` mutable str, `prevented` flag. ReplacementManager only consulted in move_to_zone when `replacement_event is not None AND leaving_battlefield`.\n   - move_to_zone (zones.py): handles leaving/entering battlefield hooks; fires events BEFORE unregister; registers triggers/replacement effects + ETB on entering. move_zone deletes `colors_spent` on zone change.\n   - Casting (casting.py): cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` after payment. cast_spell_free casts without paying from any zone. _resolve_spell sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`, calls on_resolve, then moves permanents→battlefield or instant/sorcery→graveyard (via move_to_zone, NO replacement_event, NOT leaving battlefield).\n   - ManaPool: `last_payment_colors` (list[Color], colorless excluded, sorted); pay() works on a copy then commits. No total-mana-spent tracking exists.\n   - copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets) for casualty/storm.\n   - Loyalty: LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description); LoyaltyAbilityInstance + activate_ability enforce sorcery-speed + once-per-turn (clear_loyalty_tracking). _resolve_target / _resolve_ backdoor used by Kaito loyalty.\n   - ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description); ActivatedAbilityInstance; tap_cost helper.\n   - ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description); resolves immediately.\n   - Continuous effects: ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration); Layer IntEnum (POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), SubLayer (MODIFY_PT etc.), DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0/DURATION_PERMANENT=-1. effect_manager.apply_all calls _reset_characteristics on all battlefield objects then applies sorted effects. Cleanup step calls remove_expired then apply_all.\n   - Creature._reset_characteristics resets modified_power/toughness to base, counters to base, clears _cant_*, clears `protections`. CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets card_types to _original_card_types and keywords to _original_keywords.\n   - Converge duality: real pipeline sets colors_spent as a list; FDN converge tests set it as int (e.g. WardensOfTheCycle defaults self.colors_spent:int=0). Impls must handle both (use len if list, else int).\n   - Counterspell pattern (fdn_153): can_cast scans game.stack.objects() for a non-self spell; get_targets returns the StackObject(s) with TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK); on_resolve calls _counter_spell which pops the StackObject from game.stack._items, removes card from controller's STACK zone, adds to owner's graveyard. Helper _get_chosen_target reads chosen_targets[0] then falls back to _resolve_target.\n   - GameState has `extra_turns: list[int]` (FIFO seat indices) and `_normal_next_index`; advance_phase handles end-of-turn rotation, empties mana pools each transition. No turn-skip support exists.\n   - Color enum has W/U/B/R/G aliases; ManaType includes COLORLESS. Supertype.LEGENDARY. Keyword Flag includes FLYING, REACH, HASTE, DEATHTOUCH, VIGILANCE, PROWESS, etc. (no AFFINITY/CASUALTY/MIRACLE/CONVERGE/PARADIGM/PREPARED/SURVEIL keywords).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`: constraints + layout. FDN cards with tests.py: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py`: All event dataclasses. SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller); AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker); BeginningOfMainPhase does NOT exist (would need adding). MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination=\"graveyard\", controller, owner, prevented=False, card property).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py`: cast_spell (step 8 pushes StackObject; line 229 sets colors_spent; line 232 calls on_cast). cast_spell_free. _resolve_spell (lines 378-410) — moves instant/sorcery to graveyard at line 410 with `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`. PLAN: add `card.mana_spent = total_before - total_after` after pay; fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent after pushing stack_obj; in _resolve_spell route to EXILE when `getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False)`; apply casualty after pushing stack_obj.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py`: declare_attackers_step (lines 208-257) sets attacker.is_attacking=True, taps unless VIGILANCE — does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent. PLAN: fire AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker) for each declared attacker.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py`: CardImpl, Creature (base_power/toughness, modified_*, power/toughness properties incl counters, _reset_characteristics), Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker(starting_loyalty, loyalty, get_loyalty_abilities), Land(can_cast→False, get_mana_abilities). Dataclasses Mode, ActivatedAbility, LoyaltyAbility, ManaAbility, ContinuousEffect (note: card.py's ContinuousEffect has apply/remove/description — DIFFERENT from continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect which has source/layer/sublayer/apply/timestamp/duration; use the latter for effect_manager.add).\n   - `/workspace/engine/types.py`: Color, ManaType, Zone, Phase, Step, CardType, Supertype, Keyword, ManaCost(parse/cmc/generic/pips/x_count/hybrid), TargetRequirement.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py`: deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card, discard, create_token (sets is_token, fires ETB, registers triggers), add_counter/remove_counter (\"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\"), tap/untap, run_game.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py`: move_to_zone semantics as above.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py`: activate_ability, ActivatedAbilityInstance, LoyaltyAbilityInstance, tap_cost, loyalty per-turn tracking.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py`: advance_phase, extra_turns, _normal_next_index, empty_mana_pools. _TURN_SEQUENCE imported by test_utils.\n   - `/workspace/engine/continuous_effects.py`: EffectManager.add/remove_expired/apply_all, Layer, SubLayer, durations.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py`: run_turn; fires BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent in upkeep (line ~204); main phases have step=None and currently fire nothing. PLAN: optionally fire a new BeginningOfMainPhase event here for Mana Sculpt delayed mana.\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py`: ManaPool (add/empty/total/get/can_pay/pay/last_payment_colors).\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py`: SBA checks — _sba_creature_zero_toughness checks `hasattr(obj,'toughness') and obj.toughness <= 0` (CRITICAL for Great Hall: must NOT expose toughness when not animated). legend rule, lethal damage, etc.\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py`: create_game(deck1,deck2,*,scripts), set_board_state(game,idx,*,battlefield,hand,graveyard,life,mana), cast_spell(game,idx,name,targets) (scripts targets via player._script.appendleft), advance_to_phase, declare_attackers (scripts active player choose), declare_blockers, card_colors. _resolve_top_of_stack pops+resolves until empty.\n   - FDN references read: fdn_244 Progenitus (ProtectionAbility, _init_protection reapplied in _reset_characteristics, register_replacement_effects with MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, condition `event.card is source`, replacement shuffles to library + sets prevented=True); fdn_205 WardensOfTheCycle (converge int colors_spent, range loop create_token Saproling); fdn_153 EssenceScatter (counterspell pattern + _counter_spell + _get_chosen_target); fdn_13 FleetingFlight (TargetRequirement battlefield, add_counter + sync _base_plus_one_counters, ContinuousEffect flying EOT); fdn_44 Kaito (Planeswalker: register_triggers for DealsDamageTriggeredEvent, get_loyalty_abilities returns [LoyaltyAbility(+1,...),(-2),(-9)], emblem via `type('Emblem',(),{...})()` + SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger); fdn_95 Sower (get_activated_abilities with cost paying mana_pool.pay, effect uses _current_target); fdn_245 Ruby (register_triggers AttacksTriggeredEvent with `event.creature is source`, get_mana_abilities with _tap_cost); fdn_215 Bushwhack (get_modes + self.chosen_mode, library search + fight via deal_damage).\n   - All 10 SOS stubs are bare `class X(CardImpl): pass`. Specs captured below in Pending/design.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None — no code has been written or executed yet this session. No errors encountered.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed via grep that AttacksTriggeredEvent/SpellCastTriggeredEvent are defined but never fired; Ruby/Kaito register them — so firing them is the intended additive change. engine_tests/test_triggers.py tests TriggerManager directly and test_combat.py calls declare_attackers_step many times; firing events is a no-op without matching triggers, so safe.\n   - Determined total mana spent must be added as `card.mana_spent` (computed as pool total before minus after pay) for Mana Sculpt.\n   - Identified that the exile-instead-of-graveyard for The Dawning Archaic's free-cast spell won't trigger via normal replacement path (resolution leaves STACK not battlefield, no replacement_event passed) — plan to route via a `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag checked in _resolve_spell (additive body modification).\n   - Designed a generic additive cost-reduction hook in get_cost_reduction iterating battlefield permanents for `static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` to support Witherbloom granting affinity to other spells.\n   - Designed a casualty mechanism (new file engine/casualty.py) with `grant_casualty(game, card, controller)` permanent hook + apply_casualty creating a copy via copy_spell, for Silverquill.\n   - Great Hall animation: must NOT expose power/toughness attributes when un-animated (SBA would kill it / combat would consider it). Plan: set creature attrs only on animate, update _original_card_types to include CREATURE, override _reset_characteristics to reset power/toughness to base when animated; cast-trigger +1/+0 increments self.power AND registers an EOT MODIFY_PT ContinuousEffect that re-adds +1 after reset.\n   - Ral Zarek −7 turn-skip: no engine support; plan a guarded additive skip in advance_phase keyed on a `skip_turns` player attribute (never set in existing tests, so safe); coin flips via random (seed in own tests).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Resumed-session system context with prior summary; not a new instruction.)\n   - Repeated automated system-reminders: \"The task tools haven't been used recently... consider using TaskCreate/TaskUpdate...\" and listing the 13 existing tasks.\n   - Original task (from prior summary, still governing): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks (tracked as tasks #1–#13):\n   - #1 Engine: fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent + track `card.mana_spent` in cast_spell/cast_spell_free.\n   - #2 Engine: fire AttacksTriggeredEvent in declare_attackers_step.\n   - #3 SOS 245 Witherbloom (affinity via cost_reduction + static_cost_reduction hook): {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Flying Deathtouch Legendary Elder Dragon; affinity for creatures (self + your instant/sorcery spells).\n   - #4 SOS 4 Together as One: Sorcery {6}, converge — target player draws X, deal X to any target, gain X life; X=colors spent (handle list or int).\n   - #5 SOS 57 Mana Sculpt: Instant {1}{U}{U}, counter target spell; if you control a Wizard, add {C} = mana spent to cast that spell at beginning of your next main phase (delayed via new BeginningOfMainPhase event + one-shot trigger).\n   - #6 SOS 1 The Dawning Archa