ests) and test_combat.py (declare_attackers_step calls), so firing AttacksTriggeredEvent/SpellCastTriggeredEvent in combat/casting is safe; and (b) fdn_194 is the only FDN card matching two-faced search terms. In its private reasoning, the assistant finalized concrete implementation designs for every engine change and all 10 cards (detailed in sections 3, 5, and 7 above). No files have been created or edited yet. The 13-task list has been created (all still pending). The next action would be to begin editing engine files and then card impls.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementation, starting with the two engine changes that unblock multiple cards, directly per the user's instruction that \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics.\" Concretely: (1) edit `engine/casting.py` to fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after pushing the spell's StackObject and to set `card.mana_spent` (pool total before minus after payment) in both `cast_spell` and `cast_spell_free`, plus route instant/sorcery resolution in `_resolve_spell` to EXILE when `getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False)` is set; (2) edit `engine/combat.py` `declare_attackers_step` to fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` for each declared attacker. Then implement cards in order of complexity (SOS 245 Witherbloom affinity first via a new `static_cost_reduction` hook added additively to `get_cost_reduction`), followed by SOS 4, 57, 1, 226, 201, 13, 120, 97, 257, writing `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` for each, and finally running `pytest`. Before any edits, re-confirm not touching `engine_tests/` or FDN `tests.py`, and mark task #1 in_progress via TaskUpdate.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/735f529e-7bc8-4328-a211-d2f095818fd0.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"735f529e-7bc8-4328-a211-d2f095818fd0","uuid":"908d04c9-d426-4328-9795-98fd82b6f267","timestamp":"2026-06-04T09:54:41.335Z","isSynthetic":true}
