{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a stub `card_impl.py` (`class X(CardImpl): pass`) to complete. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Consult `RULEBOOK.txt` via grep (never read whole). The agent is \"expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics\" and is \"free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\" Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. Run tests from workspace root with `pytest` (the available interpreter is `python3`, not `python`).\n\n   Hard constraints (MUST be preserved verbatim):\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Do NOT modify or delete existing FDN reference test files at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (read for examples only).\n   - Engine modifications are ADDITIVE-ONLY: may add new methods/classes/helpers/files in `engine/` and may modify the bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/`.\n   - Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; do not move/rename card directories.\n   - Per-card SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - pytest.ini sets `python_files = test_*.py tests.py`, 5-minute per-test timeout.\n\n   Final user message: produce a TEXT-ONLY summary (no tool calls).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Layered MTG engine: CardImpl/Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Planeswalker/Land hierarchy, GameState, Stack/StackObject, TriggerManager, ReplacementManager, EffectManager (7-layer continuous effects), CombatState, ManaPool, DeterministicPlayer.\n   - Card hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)` (generic-only, clamped ≥0), `on_cast`, `on_resolve` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets` (returns list[TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)]), `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, Planeswalker `get_loyalty_abilities`, Land `get_mana_abilities`.\n   - NEW hooks I introduced (called from engine additively): `static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller) -> int` (battlefield permanent grants generic reduction to a spell being cast) and `grants_casualty(game, card, controller) -> int` (battlefield permanent grants casualty N).\n   - get_cost_reduction now: sets card.controller, calls card.cost_reduction(game), restores; then ADDS `permanent.static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` for each battlefield permanent (skip the card itself); clamps `max(0, min(raw, generic))`.\n   - cast_spell now sets `card.mana_spent = total_before - total_after`, fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player, card, controller=player)` after push, and calls `_apply_casualty(game, card, player, stack_obj)`. cast_spell_free sets `card.mana_spent = 0` and fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - _resolve_spell: permanents→battlefield; else if `getattr(card,\"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\",False)` → STACK→EXILE; else STACK→GRAVEYARD.\n   - `_apply_casualty(game, card, controller, stack_obj)`: only instant/sorcery; N=max over battlefield grants_casualty hooks; eligible = controller's creatures with power≥N (excluding card); choose_yes_no, choose creature, `from engine.game import sacrifice; from engine.stack import copy_spell`; sacrifice then push copy. Returns early (no script consumption) when N≤0 — so cards/tests without a grantor are unaffected.\n   - copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None): shallow-copies card, binds resolve to copied_card.on_resolve, sets copied_card.chosen_targets at resolve.\n   - TriggerManager.fire_event returns early when no triggers match (no-op) — so firing SpellCastTriggeredEvent/AttacksTriggeredEvent/BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent is safe for existing tests. register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)); unregister(source) is identity-based; effect becomes the pushed StackObject.on_resolve.\n   - move_to_zone: only consults ReplacementManager when replacement_event AND leaving_battlefield; unregisters triggers/replacements ONLY when leaving battlefield; spell resolution (STACK→GRAVEYARD/EXILE) does NOT leave battlefield, so triggers with source=self persist.\n   - ManaPool.last_payment_colors: already a list of distinct Colors (built from set, sorted), colorless excluded → `len(card.colors_spent)` gives distinct color count. _auto_pay_generic pays colorless first then colored in enum order — paying {N} with only colored mana registers those colors.\n   - Converge handling: `_converge_x()` returns `len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list) else int(cs)` (real pipeline sets list; tests may set int).\n   - draw_card increments player.cards_drawn_this_turn (NEVER reset anywhere) and fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent.\n   - turn.py run_turn: untap clears summoning_sick + land_plays_remaining=1; upkeep fires BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (no player field — use game.active_player in condition; opponent's upkeep = `game.active_player is not controller`); NOW also fires BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player) at both main phases; priority granted except Untap/Cleanup; advance_phase empties mana pools on every transition.\n   - test_utils.cast_spell prepends reversed(targets) to player._script, then auto-resolves entire stack via _resolve_top_of_stack (pop+on_resolve+SBA loop). Additional choices (casualty yes/no, sac creature; miracle yes/no) must be in the base script AFTER prepended targets. set_board_state bypasses move_to_zone → register_triggers/register_replacement_effects NOT called automatically; tests must call card.register_triggers(game) manually for trigger-based behavior. declare_attackers prepends [attackers] to active player's script and calls declare_attackers_step (which now fires AttacksTriggeredEvent but does NOT resolve the pushed trigger — must resolve stack manually after).\n   - Keyword Flag enum (FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS) — NO AFFINITY/CASUALTY/MIRACLE/CONVERGE keyword; implement via hooks, do not add to keywords enum.\n   - Supertype.LEGENDARY for legendary cards; Elder Dragon subtypes = {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` (EDITED):\n     - get_cost_reduction now iterates `for permanent in list(controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all()): if permanent is card: continue; hook=getattr(permanent,\"static_cost_reduction\",None); if hook is None: continue; raw += hook(game, card, controller)` before clamping.\n     - cast_spell payment block: `total_before = player.mana_pool.total(); player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost); card.mana_spent = total_before - player.mana_pool.total()`. After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`: `_apply_casualty(game, card, player, stack_obj)` then `from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent; game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`.\n     - cast_spell_free: `card.mana_spent = 0` before on_cast; after push fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent identically.\n     - Added `_apply_casualty(game, card, controller, stack_obj)` between cast_spell_free and _resolve_spell.\n     - _resolve_spell adds the